---
title: Git snapshots preserve exported content
---

# Git snapshots preserve exported content

Git owns commit history and pinned source blobs. `.brain/data/git-snapshot.json` is a derived build input for exported trees.

- `pnpm git-snapshot` is its only writer. Run it in a full checkout.
- The content build collects the queries it uses and fingerprints their source files.
- Blob records carry the Git object ID. The reader checks the Git blob checksum.
- Checkout builds recompute each query and compare the result with the snapshot.
- Exported builds read the snapshot after `git rev-parse --git-dir` returns a nonzero status.
- Missing records, changed fingerprints, and checksum failures stop the build with a repair command.
- Drift still compares the pinned excerpt with the recorded HEAD source. Differences remain warnings.

## Commit boundary

The snapshot tracks rendered law, skill, and lore paths, plus pinned source paths. It does not track itself or generated assets.

Commit content changes before regenerating the snapshot. Then commit the snapshot. Its commit changes no tracked history, so it stays fresh.

A documentation commit outside rendered paths needs no refresh. A commit that changes rendered content requires one because its history output changes.

## Check

Run `pnpm turbo run check test build --concurrency=1` in both a checkout and its exported tree. Compare generated source files and static assets byte for byte.

The boundary property exercises both readers with generated blob text. It also checks missing queries and changed source fingerprints.

The content version excludes all generated TypeScript modules. A cold export lacks the generated icon module before its first build. Hashing that module made warm and cold output differ.

## Gate resource use

The gate serializes package tasks. Mischief also serializes its test files.

The previous worker count used half the available cores: eight workers in the measured environment. The unchanged filesystem property exceeded its five-second budget twice under concurrent load.

The single-worker probe passed all 51 files and 444 tests in 51.04 seconds. It kept every property run and timeout unchanged. The slower suite reduces contention instead of weakening assertions.

Source: `apps/mischief/scripts/git-snapshot.ts`, `apps/mischief/test/git-snapshot.test.ts`, `apps/mischief/vitest.config.ts`.
